1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:03,380
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:32,260
[Yuru breathes shakily]

3
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:36,810
[Yuru sighs]

4
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,180
[YURU] You've got one of those
smoke signal things, right?

5
00:01:41,270 --> 00:01:42,350
[JIN] Hm?

6
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:45,610
The device that lets you talk
to people far away.

7
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:47,820
I saw you were using it earlier.

8
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:49,690
Oh, you mean my smartphone.

9
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,530
You're gonna tell Asa
to come here.

10
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:55,950
I just want to talk,
that's all.

11
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,870
All that you wanna do is talk?

12
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:03,290
Yeah, I figured he'd be
telling us to hand her over,

13
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:05,960
-"or else."
-Why settle for a simple chat?

14
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:08,340
Surely Higashi Village
wants both twins.

15
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:10,000
But that's not why I'm here.

16
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:11,970
I came on my own,
for my own reasons.

17
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,800
All right,
then let's continue this

18
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,220
at the Kagemori manor.

19
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,060
Asa has been wanting
to see you, too,

20
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,470
and you can talk there.

21
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:22,310
Only a fool would walk
willingly into a bear's den.

22
00:02:22,390 --> 00:02:23,520
Have her come here.

23
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:26,020
And stop acting like
this is a negotiation

24
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:27,480
because it really isn't.

25
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:29,110
Hey, kid, tell you what.

26
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,070
Why don't you at least
let us see what we can do

27
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,240
about that wound you gave him?

28
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,740
He could bleed out.

29
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:37,160
I made sure it wasn't
deep enough to kill him.

30
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,530
But very well.

31
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:40,490
You kept it shallow on purpose?

32
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:41,790
Jin, isn't it?

33
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,960
You trapped me, but that's it.

34
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,580
I didn't sense bloodlust
in you.

35
00:02:45,670 --> 00:02:46,710
[JIN] Hm.

36
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:48,380
[YURU] If you had
wanted to kill me,

37
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,130
things would have
turned out much differently.

38
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:53,800
[HARUO] You'd think
mountain folk would be peaceful.

39
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,880
But this kid's terrifying.

40
00:02:56,970 --> 00:02:58,090
[YURU] It's true.

41
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:59,510
If he had wanted me dead,

42
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,640
he would have seen to it
with that first attack.

43
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:10,650
[RIGHT] The fish belong
to the spectacled one.

44
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:13,990
And the hare and tortoise
answer to the rumpled youth.

45
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,820
There's another pair somewhere,

46
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,320
though they have yet
to show themselves.

47
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:18,950
Yours, I assume?

48
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:21,080
Yeah. Those two would be mine.

49
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,080
They aren't far.

50
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,910
And yet they didn't aid you
in the fight?

51
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:27,250
Are they not suited
to combat, then?

52
00:03:27,330 --> 00:03:30,210
Oh, suitability
is not the issue.

53
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:32,040
[ALL] Hmm?

54
00:03:34,550 --> 00:03:37,180
It's just, they're too big
to fit in here.

55
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,800
If you want, though,

56
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:41,100
-I could make them try.
-[Yuru whimpers]

57
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:44,140
I fear bringing Asa here
is out of the question.

58
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:46,020
But if you'll let us
take you back with us

59
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:48,980
to the Kagemori manor,
no harm will come to you.

60
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:50,650
You have my word on that.

61
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:53,900
Killing you isn't my objective.

62
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:55,490
You just said as much yourself.

63
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:58,240
[Yuru breathes uneasily]

64
00:03:58,950 --> 00:04:02,200
[YURU] The hare and tortoise,
plus whatever that is.

65
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,580
Left and Right
might be outmatched.

66
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,960
[YURU] Fine, I'll go
to this manor of yours.

67
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,460
But I want Left and Right
to be treated

68
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:14,800
with respect while we're there.

69
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,880
And they will be.

70
00:04:17,970 --> 00:04:21,140
You're coming as our guests,
not our prisoners.

71
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:23,600
[YURU] Then let's stop talking
and move.

72
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:24,930
Take us to Asa.

73
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:28,560
[JIN] Actually, we need
to clean up a bit first.

74
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:32,980
Ai, my dear, think you can
handle this for us?

75
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,980
[Ai growls]

76
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:40,570
As usual, Scavenger makes
a mess wherever they go.

77
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:42,120
You mean the fish?

78
00:04:42,570 --> 00:04:44,280
[JIN] Scavenger.

79
00:04:44,370 --> 00:04:45,990
Nature's janitors.

80
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:47,750
Ai will eat whatever I ask.

81
00:04:48,370 --> 00:04:51,290
Makoto stores those items
and summons them.

82
00:04:53,330 --> 00:04:56,130
I regularly feed them things
that might come in handy,

83
00:04:56,210 --> 00:04:58,340
so I'm prepared
in any situation.

84
00:04:59,010 --> 00:05:00,720
Though, since they're janitors,

85
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:04,050
I sometimes feed them trash
the world's better off without.

86
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:05,430
They're quite convenient.

87
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:09,230
It makes security a breeze, too,
no matter what gear I've got.

88
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:11,440
I could carry enough
for a hit or a hijacking,

89
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,060
and no one would have a clue.

90
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:15,650
That was a lot of words
that don't make sense to me,

91
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:17,440
but I get your daemons
are useful.

92
00:05:18,610 --> 00:05:19,940
[LEFT] And your daemons?

93
00:05:20,030 --> 00:05:21,200
Uh, mine?

94
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,780
The tortoise to start.

95
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,280
How many kan is it?

96
00:05:24,370 --> 00:05:26,620
[HARUO] Kan? Right.

97
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,410
How many kilograms
is that again?

98
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,660
Not that it matters,

99
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:31,210
'cause I've never actually
weighed them.

100
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:32,330
But I can tell you,

101
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:34,710
this isn't
the heaviest they get.

102
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:43,590
I require more training
before our next encounter.

103
00:05:44,090 --> 00:05:46,850
[gasps]
She is one serious fighter!

104
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:48,260
[BUNBUN] Hm?

105
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:52,020
[Right grunts softly]

106
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:53,940
[Bunbun grunts]

107
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:55,270
[Right grunts]

108
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:58,650
Yuru, are you any good
at rabbit hunting?

109
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:01,150
Sure am. I like to catch them
with snares.

110
00:06:01,610 --> 00:06:03,780
Once they're skinned,
they make good broth.

111
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,620
Barbarian!

112
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:08,240
Can daemons be eaten?
Hypothetically, I mean.

113
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,790
Uh, hello?
Is somebody in there?

114
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:13,290
Oh, good! Security.
We can use some help here.

115
00:06:13,370 --> 00:06:14,960
We're not sure
what may have caused it,

116
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,790
but the lights just went out
all of a sudden.

117
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:20,050
Hmm... Uh?
What happened to them?

118
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:22,720
They're not just off.
They're broken.

119
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,760
[HARUO]
Maybe they short-circuited.

120
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,470
We heard some crackling,
and it freaked us out a bit.

121
00:06:27,550 --> 00:06:29,060
[SECURITY] I see.

122
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:32,430
Fortunately, the lights
are still on in the stairwell.

123
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:34,020
You can exit through here.

124
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:35,640
[ALL] 'Kay...

125
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:37,520
We appreciate it.
Thank you!

126
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:41,530
[phone vibrating]

127
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:43,490
[Asa grunts softly]

128
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,570
[Asa groans softly]

129
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:51,790
[Asa gasps]

130
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,750
Gabby! Gabby! Gabby!
Gabby! Gabby! Gabby!

131
00:06:55,830 --> 00:06:57,500
What? We under attack?

132
00:06:57,580 --> 00:07:00,590
[ASA] No, look!
Jin is bringing my brother here.

133
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,050
[GABBY] Seriously?
That dude works fast.

134
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:06,130
I'm not ready, though!
What am I going to wear?

135
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:07,840
Uh, I don't know, clothes?

136
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:09,220
Does it matter?

137
00:07:13,390 --> 00:07:16,140
[JIN] It's Jin.
Sorry to be calling so late.

138
00:07:17,190 --> 00:07:19,190
I've settled things
with the brother.

139
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,690
That's right.

140
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:22,570
I have him in the car
with me right now.

141
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,780
We're on our way
to the manor as we speak.

142
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:26,200
[YURU] How long is this cave?

143
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,860
Yeah? Nice work.

144
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:29,120
I'm impressed.

145
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:32,540
Can you keep him there a while,
at least until I make it back?

146
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:35,120
[JIN] That depends.
Where are you, sir?

147
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:37,120
[chuckles] At a hot spring.

148
00:07:38,290 --> 00:07:40,170
[GONZO] Thought I'd get
an after-work soak in,

149
00:07:40,250 --> 00:07:41,880
but this is more important.

150
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:44,170
I'll go and head that way
right now.

151
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:45,510
-You'd all better be nice...
-[camera clicks]

152
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:46,510
...to young Yuru.

153
00:08:05,690 --> 00:08:07,570
♪

154
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:16,580
Here we are.

155
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:18,710
The Kagemori clan home.

156
00:08:20,290 --> 00:08:21,500
♪

157
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,850
[RIGHT] We were
to understand the Kagemoris

158
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:41,980
had a goodly number
of Daemon Wielders.

159
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:45,020
Yet I sense none of my kind.

160
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:46,650
There are plenty of them around.

161
00:08:47,490 --> 00:08:50,030
We're just not
in the VIP area yet.

162
00:08:50,490 --> 00:08:52,700
-[LEFT] VIP?
-[JIN] Limited access.

163
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:55,160
We'll be crossing the barrier
in a moment.

164
00:08:59,910 --> 00:09:01,290
[Yuru grunts uneasily]

165
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:17,770
-Yes.
-Incredible.

166
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:20,350
[RIGHT] Daemons everywhere.

167
00:09:20,430 --> 00:09:23,150
So many I can't even count
the number of pairs.

168
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:26,190
-[Gabriel grumbles]
-Hm?

169
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,530
Jin is pulling up into the drive
with your brother.

170
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:30,650
Now?

171
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,740
You wanna go with me
to greet him?

172
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:34,740
He put literal holes in my body,

173
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:37,370
so I'm gonna pass
on that invite, thanks.

174
00:09:37,450 --> 00:09:39,700
Every step
still reminds me of him.

175
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:41,710
Okay. Wish me luck.

176
00:09:42,210 --> 00:09:43,330
[GABBY] Go get him, girl!

177
00:09:44,330 --> 00:09:46,750
I'm gonna get some sleep.

178
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:48,590
[Jiro grunts softly]

179
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:59,390
[DERA] Is that one
enormous building?

180
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:01,020
[HANA] Or a giant plot of land?

181
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:02,600
[Kotetsu grunts]

182
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:03,770
[HANA AND DERA] Hm?

183
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,770
[both groaning]

184
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:12,360
[HANA] Oh!
Did he get himself captured?

185
00:10:12,950 --> 00:10:14,450
[DERA] Wouldn't have
thought that was possible

186
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:16,450
with Left and Right
guarding him.

187
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,370
Well, nothin' for it.

188
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:21,450
I'll go rescue our wayward son
from whatever trouble he's in.

189
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:23,710
[HANA] Want me to drive you?

190
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:26,580
[DERA] Nah, they don't know
we're associated yet.

191
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:28,500
Might as well keep it that way.

192
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,170
I'll just catch a cab.

193
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:32,720
And how will you get home?

194
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:34,680
[DERA] By train.

195
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:37,930
Yuru can learn about the joys
of public transportation.

196
00:10:38,010 --> 00:10:39,640
[door opens, closes]

197
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:48,820
[YURU] What a huge entryway!

198
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,770
[RIGHT] Like a castle
upon the plains.

199
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,190
[ASUMA] Out burning
the midnight oil?

200
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,950
Ever the hard worker, Jin.

201
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:59,030
[HARUO] Asuma, how are you?

202
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,160
[JIN] Why are you out so late?

203
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,830
I heard that the other twin
would be arriving soon,

204
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:06,120
so I came to extend a greeting.

205
00:11:07,130 --> 00:11:09,340
I don't believe you were
among the people I told.

206
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:10,670
[Asuma chuckles]

207
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:12,670
I have quite excellent hearing.

208
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:13,880
Oh, my!

209
00:11:13,970 --> 00:11:15,220
You're injured.

210
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,510
It's nothing the doc
can't fix up for me.

211
00:11:18,180 --> 00:11:20,800
Then I presume you got
in a fight with them?

212
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:23,890
Oh, what beautiful daemons!

213
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:27,140
And you, my friend,
are Asa's brother?

214
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:30,110
[Asuma chuckles]

215
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:32,980
I'm Asuma Kagemori.
At your service.

216
00:11:33,070 --> 00:11:35,240
[Asa panting] Are you here?

217
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,910
It is you.

218
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,910
You're alive?
You're not dead?

219
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,250
[YURU] Who greets
someone like that?

220
00:11:47,330 --> 00:11:48,790
Can I please give you a hug?

221
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,000
[YURU] Not so fast!

222
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,550
[Asa cries] Sorry, I don't know
how close we should be.

223
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:54,800
Neither do I.

224
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:58,470
I didn't come here
hoping to repair old bonds.

225
00:11:58,550 --> 00:12:00,800
I'm here to get some
answers out of you.

226
00:12:01,430 --> 00:12:02,800
You can ask me anything.

227
00:12:02,890 --> 00:12:04,770
Then once we're done,
can I hug you?

228
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:05,850
[YURU] I said no!

229
00:12:06,390 --> 00:12:08,810
[ASA] Oh! Oh, my gosh.
You grew up into such a badass!

230
00:12:09,850 --> 00:12:12,980
Look, forget me.
Worry about this guy.

231
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:15,530
Whoa! You need to get
to the infirmary!

232
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:18,150
His injury gives us
the perfect excuse.

233
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:20,410
Why don't I take you on
a little tour around the manor?

234
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:23,120
[ASA] Oh, I didn't
see you there, Asuma.

235
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:26,160
Wow. Quite the tunnel vision
for your big brother.

236
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:28,000
I invited Yuru here,

237
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,120
so I'll be seeing to his stay.

238
00:12:30,210 --> 00:12:31,880
You have no business
with our guest.

239
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,460
Very well, then.

240
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,010
Welcome. Please,
treat this place like home.

241
00:12:42,510 --> 00:12:45,930
Akio, you're on guard
outside the barrier.

242
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:47,270
Let no one in.

243
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:48,810
Sir.

244
00:12:49,350 --> 00:12:50,520
[JIN] As for you,

245
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:53,230
as long as you're at the manor,
I want you close to me.

246
00:12:53,310 --> 00:12:55,820
Can't have you getting lost.

247
00:12:57,650 --> 00:12:59,200
♪

248
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,700
[SAKURAZAWA] Oh, yeah.

249
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:05,200
That one's gonna need
some stitches.

250
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:07,160
Wait. You're kidding!

251
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:08,830
A billhook?

252
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:10,160
Straight to the calf.

253
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:12,500
[SAKURAZAWA] I was wondering
what was urgent enough

254
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:14,340
to wake me up so late.

255
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:17,210
Can't believe you got caught
by some kid with a machete.

256
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:20,470
-Teenagers are scary these days.
-[keyboard tapping]

257
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:21,970
Well, most teenagers

258
00:13:22,050 --> 00:13:23,970
aren't carrying hunting weapons,
you know?

259
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:27,970
Seriously? What kind of kid
doesn't have a billhook or two?

260
00:13:28,060 --> 00:13:29,810
Absolutely.

261
00:13:29,890 --> 00:13:31,730
[HARUO] Twin barbarians!

262
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:34,900
Hey, doc, I'm done
with Asa's blood.

263
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,440
I brought it back for you.

264
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,780
[SAKURAZAWA] Don't make a habit
of carrying that stuff.

265
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,400
-It's unsanitary.
-[Yuru gasps]

266
00:13:40,490 --> 00:13:42,150
Almost forgot!

267
00:13:42,240 --> 00:13:43,910
What kind of fiend
would draw blood

268
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:45,120
from a young lady like that?

269
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:47,950
It was my idea for Jin
to take my blood,

270
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,830
so try not to judge him for it.

271
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:52,250
Modern medicine's crazy.
Because of it,

272
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:55,290
we can bleed someone
without cutting a single vein.

273
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,840
[YURU] Really?
What kind of sorcery--

274
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,590
[JIN] Her blood
was drawn safely.

275
00:13:59,670 --> 00:14:01,510
We did it in this infirmary.

276
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,720
[SAKURAZAWA]
We use this. It's harmless.

277
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,970
[ASA] If a doctor's skilled,
then you don't feel anything.

278
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:08,850
[YURU] This heinous practice
is medicine?

279
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,640
[HARUO]
Didn't he cut open Jin's leg?

280
00:14:11,730 --> 00:14:13,690
This is where he draws the line?

281
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:15,860
He's got some messed up morals.

282
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:17,730
The Kagemori clan gives me food

283
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:19,440
and keeps me safe
inside their walls,

284
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:21,780
so a little blood felt like
the least I could give back.

285
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,620
Would it be okay for me
to hug you now?

286
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:29,030
[grunts] No way!

287
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:31,500
I still can't get over
how big you are!

288
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,000
The Asa I know is tiny

289
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,750
and cute
and couldn't hurt a fly!

290
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:35,920
Aw, don't worry.

291
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,920
You'll grow bigger too
if you keep eating the food

292
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
they have down here!

293
00:14:39,090 --> 00:14:41,170
I don't like it. Too salty.

294
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:42,720
Oh, you think?

295
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:44,630
[YURU] And too heavily seasoned!

296
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:46,090
Maybe I'm just used to it

297
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:47,970
after living down here
for so long.

298
00:14:48,050 --> 00:14:50,560
The rice here is great!
I'll grant you that.

299
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,230
Hold on. I didn't come here
to talk about food.

300
00:14:53,310 --> 00:14:54,940
[ASA] Right! You said you have

301
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,850
-questions for me, yeah?
-[YURU] Yeah.

302
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,440
[ASA] And after I answer,
then can I hug you?

303
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:02,190
[YURU] Gotta hand it to you,
you sure don't give up!

304
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,110
[HARUO] They're pretty in sync.

305
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,610
Must be a twin thing.

306
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,990
You're gonna tell me
where Mom and Dad are.

307
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,540
[Asa gasps softly]

308
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:13,870
Let me see them.

309
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,870
You fled the village together,
didn't you?

310
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:23,130
-Then...
-[ASA] They're not here.

311
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:24,880
Where are they?

312
00:15:26,130 --> 00:15:27,300
I wish I knew.

313
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:28,850
[Yuru gasps softly]

314
00:15:28,930 --> 00:15:31,680
[ASA] Unfortunately,
they're missing.

315
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:35,850
♪

316
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,360
[JIN] How much
should I tell him?

317
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:44,490
All of it.

318
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,700
After everything,
I refuse to lie to my brother.

319
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,030
[Jin sighs softly]

320
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,750
Your parents didn't have
an easy go of things

321
00:15:57,830 --> 00:15:59,830
after they fled the village.

322
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:03,590
So they came to the Kagemoris
seeking protection.

323
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:05,720
Took a while to settle in.

324
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,170
But once they finally had,

325
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:09,470
they decided to pay a visit
to your mother's home.

326
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:11,510
That's right.

327
00:16:11,930 --> 00:16:14,890
My mother told me she was born
in a place down the mountain.

328
00:16:14,970 --> 00:16:17,270
She said she wanted
to take me there.

329
00:16:17,350 --> 00:16:19,690
[JIN] Your mother's from a place
called Okinawa.

330
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,110
[ASA] It's an island

331
00:16:21,190 --> 00:16:23,020
far to the south
of the mainland.

332
00:16:23,570 --> 00:16:26,280
You would need a boat
or a plane to get there.

333
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,320
[YURU] What's a "plane?"

334
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,950
We called them "dragons"
in the village.

335
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:33,410
[YURU] You mean
those are vehicles?

336
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:36,290
[ASA] Yes, and they carry
more than a hundred people.

337
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:39,330
Mom had family here,
and as far as they knew,

338
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:41,790
she went missing
in some mountains in Tohoku.

339
00:16:41,880 --> 00:16:43,840
She was hoping
to show her own parents

340
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:45,420
that she was still alive,

341
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,220
so she left me here
in the care of the Kagemoris.

342
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:51,760
They boarded the plane
to Okinawa, but didn't land.

343
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:54,260
They're gone.

344
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:55,430
[Yuru gasps softly]

345
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,680
[YURU] The plane...

346
00:16:58,890 --> 00:17:00,690
Could they have fallen
out of it?

347
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:01,850
[ASA] Mm-mm.

348
00:17:02,190 --> 00:17:03,980
They vanished
in midair somehow.

349
00:17:04,070 --> 00:17:05,480
The doors never opened.

350
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:09,070
We know for a fact
that they boarded in Tokyo.

351
00:17:09,150 --> 00:17:12,490
But when it landed,
they were nowhere to be found.

352
00:17:13,280 --> 00:17:15,530
[YURU] Did someone abduct them?

353
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:16,700
[ASA] We don't know.

354
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:18,450
[YURU] Why was
no one guarding them?

355
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,790
[ASA] They had a guard.

356
00:17:20,410 --> 00:17:21,710
The Kagemoris assigned

357
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,670
one of our most trusted
Daemon Wielders

358
00:17:23,750 --> 00:17:25,920
to see they
arrived there safely.

359
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:28,340
They still disappeared,
guard and all.

360
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:30,670
[gasps] About that guard...

361
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,050
Think they could have had
something to do with it?

362
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:35,470
[ASA] Yeah.
It's crossed our minds.

363
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:38,310
They could've been an enemy,
just playing the part.

364
00:17:38,930 --> 00:17:41,980
Say, an agent
from Higashi Village,

365
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:43,810
sent to infiltrate
the Kagemoris.

366
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:45,690
[Yuru grunts]

367
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:49,230
Regardless of their allegiance,
an apology is in order.

368
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:51,490
By no means
should we have lost them.

369
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:54,740
And what? You really
still trust these guys?

370
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:56,490
They lost our parents!

371
00:17:56,950 --> 00:17:58,740
After we left the village,

372
00:17:58,830 --> 00:18:01,120
their assassins hounded us
day after day

373
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,660
with seemingly no end.

374
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:05,380
There's one reason
we stayed safe all those years.

375
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:07,340
It's thanks
to the kindness of Jin

376
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:08,500
and the Kagemori clan.

377
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,510
[Yuru gasps softly]

378
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,010
So, yes, I trust them
with my life.

379
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,010
[Yuru grunting]

380
00:18:30,030 --> 00:18:32,820
[MAN 1] The boy made his way
inside Kagemori manor.

381
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:35,570
[WOMAN] Jin managed to work
faster than we expected.

382
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:37,070
[MAN 1] In 400 years,

383
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:38,830
they're the first twins
we've seen

384
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:40,620
born to sunder night and day.

385
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:45,210
[MAN 2] Four hundred years!
400 years! 400 years!

386
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:48,130
[MAN 3] They're both down here.
Away from the mountain.

387
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:50,170
[MAN 1] Our timing
couldn't be better.

388
00:18:50,250 --> 00:18:52,670
The girl with the jaw daemon
is badly injured.

389
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:53,800
[MAN 3] Jin, too.

390
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,630
[MAN 1] And the master is away.

391
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,510
[MAN 4]
What a golden opportunity.

392
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:00,470
We can easily seize
both twins at once.

393
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:01,640
[WOMAN] Easily?

394
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:03,930
There is still the boy
and his daemons.

395
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:05,520
They seem quite capable.

396
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:07,520
[MAN 2] And the girl?
What of the girl?

397
00:19:07,610 --> 00:19:09,320
Don't forget the girl!

398
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,520
[MAN 1] We're striking at night.

399
00:19:10,610 --> 00:19:12,940
She's weaker
than during the day.

400
00:19:13,030 --> 00:19:14,440
The boy is dangerous.

401
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:16,400
But we're fine to let him die.

402
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:17,870
As for the girl,

403
00:19:17,950 --> 00:19:20,120
we only need
what's above the neck!

404
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:21,580
[Right grunts]

405
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:23,240
♪

406
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,430
[squeaking]

407
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:42,520
[Gabby groaning]

408
00:19:47,690 --> 00:19:48,980
[GABBY] What?

409
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:51,940
Why'd you wake me up
before the sun's even out?

410
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:53,650
♪

411
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:58,240
[GABBY] Huh?

412
00:19:58,320 --> 00:20:00,830
I don't think we've met before.

413
00:20:00,910 --> 00:20:03,200
[Gabriel growling]

414
00:20:03,290 --> 00:20:05,160
[footsteps running]

415
00:20:09,080 --> 00:20:11,290
So much for being
treated like guests, Jin!

416
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:13,210
Looks like you led us
straight into a trap!

417
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:15,130
[JIN] No, those daemons
don't belong

418
00:20:15,210 --> 00:20:16,920
to any of the Kagemoris!

419
00:20:17,010 --> 00:20:19,340
Seems outsiders
have broken into the manor.

420
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:22,300
[LEFT] Have we leave
to take them down?

421
00:20:22,390 --> 00:20:25,140
I'd like to capture their master
alive for questioning,

422
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:26,350
if it's at all possible!

423
00:20:26,430 --> 00:20:27,890
How do you propose we do that?

424
00:20:27,980 --> 00:20:29,810
This manor is labyrinthine!

425
00:20:29,890 --> 00:20:32,150
Simply finding them
will prove a trial!

426
00:20:33,150 --> 00:20:35,820
[SAKURAZAWA] If you're going
to fight them, don't go halfway.

427
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:37,610
Be sure to confirm your kills!

428
00:20:37,690 --> 00:20:39,780
I'll be annoyed if you give me
more people to treat.

429
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,530
You call yourself a doctor,
and you're gonna talk like that?

430
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:45,240
What happens to a daemon pair
when their master dies?

431
00:20:45,330 --> 00:20:48,000
If they're not transferred
to a new master beforehand,

432
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,370
then they become strays.

433
00:20:49,460 --> 00:20:50,960
That's why,
at least for most of us,

434
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,750
we prioritize our masters!

435
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:54,670
[all screaming]

436
00:20:57,550 --> 00:20:59,510
So? What happens then?

437
00:20:59,590 --> 00:21:01,430
The daemon's contract
comes to an end,

438
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:03,930
and they're bound
to that location like a ghost.

439
00:21:04,010 --> 00:21:05,930
If no new contractor appears,

440
00:21:06,020 --> 00:21:08,060
they're likely to be
forgotten over time.

441
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:09,680
After a few decades
or centuries,

442
00:21:09,770 --> 00:21:11,690
-they usually cease to exist.
-[growling]

443
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,980
That seems too cruel to them.

444
00:21:14,060 --> 00:21:15,320
Understood.

445
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:17,360
I'll try leaving
their master alive if I can.

446
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:19,610
You were ready
to kill them outright?

447
00:21:19,690 --> 00:21:20,820
My brother's a saint!

448
00:21:21,450 --> 00:21:23,780
Jin, they have
any bow and arrows?

449
00:21:23,870 --> 00:21:24,830
Well, my boy?

450
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,000
[YURU] What is all that?

451
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,920
You can't just give me
a normal bow?

452
00:21:39,130 --> 00:21:42,930
I suppose
I'll give this one a try.

453
00:21:43,010 --> 00:21:45,390
[both growling]

454
00:21:49,270 --> 00:21:50,480
[Asa gasps]

455
00:21:55,690 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

456
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:29,990
[Asa gasps] Where's my brother?

457
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:32,200
[GABBY] You mind if I just
do my thing over here?

458
00:23:32,870 --> 00:23:35,540
[ASA] If my brother
acquires the power of Seal,

459
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:36,920
she'll be his nemesis, too.
